-- Part 3A. HYPOTHETICAL: Fay was abused at a boarding school run by a religious order in 2023, aged 13.
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse question` `sexual abuse` 13 FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is child abuse under the Act (s 3)`
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse question` `sexual abuse` 17 FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is child abuse under the Act (s 3)`
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse question` `sexual abuse` 18 FALSE EQUALS `no: child abuse must be perpetrated against a child, an individual under 18 (s 3)`
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse question` `serious physical abuse` 13 TRUE EQUALS `no: physical conduct that was lawful at the time it occurred is not child abuse (s 3(2))`
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse question` `serious physical abuse` 13 FALSE EQUALS `yes: it is child abuse under the Act (s 3)`
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse question` `psychological abuse arising from serious physical abuse` 13 TRUE EQUALS `no: physical conduct that was lawful at the time it occurred is not child abuse (s 3(2))`
-- The lawfulness carve-out is for paragraph (b) only: it does not touch sexual abuse.
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse question` `psychological abuse arising from sexual abuse` 13 TRUE EQUALS `yes: it is child abuse under the Act (s 3)`
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse question` `psychological abuse alone` 13 FALSE EQUALS `no: child abuse means sexual abuse, serious physical abuse, or psychological abuse arising from either (s 3)`
#ASSERT `Is it child abuse question` `something else (for example neglect)` 13 FALSE EQUALS `no: child abuse means sexual abuse, serious physical abuse, or psychological abuse arising from either (s 3)`

`a body` MEANS `a body, entity, body corporate, group of persons, association or organisation (incorporated or not, with or without a written constitution or fixed membership)`
#ASSERT `Is it an institution question` `a body` TRUE EQUALS `yes: Part 3A applies to it as an institution exercising care, supervision or authority over me (s 17B)`
#ASSERT `Is it an institution question` `a body` FALSE EQUALS `no: Part 3A applies to an institution only while it is exercising care, supervision or authority over the child (s 17B(1))`
#ASSERT `Is it an institution question` `a family` TRUE EQUALS `no: an institution does not include a family or an individual (s 17B(2))`
#ASSERT `Is it an institution question` `an individual` TRUE EQUALS `no: an institution does not include a family or an individual (s 17B(2))`

#ASSERT `Is the abuser associated question` `an office holder, officer, owner, trustee, employee, volunteer or contractor of the institution` EQUALS `answered` `yes: the abuser is an individual associated with the institution (s 17C(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Is the abuser associated question` `a religious leader or member of the institution, which is a religious institution` EQUALS `answered` `yes: the abuser is an individual associated with the institution (s 17C(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Is the abuser associated question` `one of those people in another institution that the institution made responsible for my care, supervision or authority` EQUALS `answered` `yes: the abuser is an individual associated with the institution (s 17C(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `Is the abuser associated question` `an individual the institution made responsible for my care, supervision or authority by an arrangement, contract or delegation` EQUALS `answered` `yes: the abuser is an individual associated with the institution (s 17C(1)(d))`
#ASSERT `Is the abuser associated question` `associated only with another institution that this institution funds or regulates` EQUALS `answered` `no: an individual is not associated with an institution only because it funds or regulates another institution they are associated with (s 17C(2))`
#ASSERT `Is the abuser associated question` `some other connection` EQUALS `not covered` `"individual associated with an institution" is an "includes" list, and further individuals may be prescribed (s 17C(1)(e)); the Regulations are not deposited and the Act does not say whether others count`

`17E onus` MEANS `yes, unless the institution proves on the balance of probabilities that it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse: once I prove the abuse by an individual associated with it while I was in its care, it is taken to have breached its duty under section 17D(1) (s 17E(2)); any award of vicarious liability under section 17G is taken into account (s 17E(5))`
`Fay's abuse` MEANS `the day` 1 6 2023
`17E probably not` MEANS `probably not: the abuse happened before Part 3A commenced (taken as 30 September 2022); section 17B(5) extends Divisions 1, 4, 5 and 6 of Part 3A to earlier causes of action but not Division 2, and the presumption against retrospective changes to liability points the same way, so the ordinary law of negligence applies; read literally, section 4(2) would reach abuse from 1 May 2003, and no court has settled which reading is right`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty question` `an individual associated with the institution` TRUE `Fay's abuse` EQUALS `17E onus`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty question` `another child in the institution's care, supervision or authority` TRUE `Fay's abuse` EQUALS `yes, unless the institution proves on the balance of probabilities that it took all reasonable steps to prevent the abuse: once I prove the abuse by another child while we were both in its care, it is taken to have breached its duty under section 17D(2) (s 17F(2)); the other child must not be named in the pleadings, and the court is closed while that child gives evidence (s 17F(5))`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty question` `an individual associated with the institution` FALSE `Fay's abuse` EQUALS `no: the reversed onus of sections 17E and 17F covers abuse only while I was under the institution's care, supervision or authority; otherwise the ordinary law of negligence applies`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty question` `someone else` TRUE `Fay's abuse` EQUALS `no: the reversed onus of sections 17E and 17F covers abuse by an individual associated with the institution or another child in its care; otherwise the ordinary law of negligence applies`
-- The commencement edges (finding 6): abuse on or after 30 September 2022 (Part 3A) is reached; abuse from 1 May 2003 to
-- 29 September 2022 is "probably not" (s 17B(5) does not name Division 2); abuse before 1 May 2003 is not reached.
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty question` `an individual associated with the institution` TRUE (`the day` 30 9 2022) EQUALS `17E onus`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty question` `an individual associated with the institution` TRUE (`the day` 29 9 2022) EQUALS `17E probably not`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty question` `another child in the institution's care, supervision or authority` TRUE (`the day` 1 6 2010) EQUALS `17E probably not`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty question` `an individual associated with the institution` TRUE (`the day` 1 5 2003) EQUALS `17E probably not`
#ASSERT `Is the institution taken to have breached its duty question` `an individual associated with the institution` TRUE (`the day` 30 4 2003) EQUALS `no: the abuse happened before the Act commenced on 1 May 2003, and section 17B(5) does not extend Divisions 2 and 3 of Part 3A to it (s 4(2))`

`vicariously liable` MEANS `yes: the institution is vicariously liable for my injury from the abuse (s 17G(1)); any award under section 17E or 17F is taken into account (s 17G(4))`
`17G does not apply` MEANS `section 17G does not make the institution liable on these facts; the general law of vicarious liability still applies (s 17G(3))`
`17G probably not` MEANS `probably not: the abuse happened before Part 3A commenced (taken as 30 September 2022); section 17B(5) extends Divisions 1, 4, 5 and 6 of Part 3A to earlier causes of action but not Division 3, and the presumption against retrospective changes to liability points the same way, so only the general law of vicarious liability applies; read literally, section 4(2) would reach abuse from 1 May 2003, and no court has settled which reading is right`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable question` `an employee of the institution` TRUE TRUE `Fay's abuse` EQUALS `vicariously liable`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable question` `someone who carried out activities that enabled the institution to perform its functions, intending to benefit it (for example a volunteer, or a priest or religious leader)` TRUE TRUE `Fay's abuse` EQUALS `vicariously liable`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable question` `a carer under a placement arrangement under section 78 of the Care and Protection of Children Act 2007 (for example a foster or kinship carer)` TRUE TRUE `Fay's abuse` EQUALS `17G does not apply`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable question` `an independent contractor working under a contract for services` TRUE TRUE `Fay's abuse` EQUALS `17G does not apply`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable question` `an employee of the institution` FALSE TRUE `Fay's abuse` EQUALS `17G does not apply`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable question` `an employee of the institution` TRUE FALSE `Fay's abuse` EQUALS `17G does not apply`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable question` `an employee of the institution` TRUE TRUE (`the day` 30 9 2022) EQUALS `vicariously liable`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable question` `an employee of the institution` TRUE TRUE (`the day` 29 9 2022) EQUALS `17G probably not`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable question` `an employee of the institution` TRUE TRUE (`the day` 1 5 2003) EQUALS `17G probably not`
#ASSERT `Is the institution vicariously liable question` `an employee of the institution` TRUE TRUE (`the day` 30 4 2003) EQUALS `no: the abuse happened before the Act commenced on 1 May 2003, and section 17B(5) does not extend Division 3 of Part 3A to it (s 4(2)); the general law of vicarious liability still applies`

-- Division 4. HYPOTHETICAL: Fay sues the order on 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Must the court appoint the nominee question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court must appoint the nominee as the proper respondent; it takes on the institution's liability to me (including for costs), is joined and conducts the defence, and may rely on the institution's defences (s 17J)`
#ASSERT `Must the court appoint the nominee question` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: the court is not required to appoint the nominee, because it is not satisfied of every matter in section 17H(2); the claim stays against the institution`
#ASSERT `Must the court appoint the nominee question` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the court is not required to appoint the nominee, because it is not satisfied of every matter in section 17H(2); the claim stays against the institution`

`Fay sues` MEANS `the day` 1 1 2026
-- 1 January 2026 + 120 days = 1 May 2026 (30 + 28 + 31 + 30 + 1); the 120 days have passed from 2 May 2026.
`Fay may apply` MEANS `yes: I may apply to the court to appoint an associated trust of the institution as the proper respondent (s 17K(1)); the institution must then, within 28 days, identify its associated trusts and their financial capacity (s 17K(3))` (`the day` 2 5 2026)
#ASSERT `Can I apply to appoint an associated trust question` `the institution did not nominate a proper respondent` `Fay sues` (`the day` 2 5 2026) EQUALS `Fay may apply`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to appoint an associated trust question` `the institution nominated one and the court did not appoint it` `Fay sues` (`the day` 1 6 2026) EQUALS `Fay may apply`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to appoint an associated trust question` `the institution did not nominate a proper respondent` `Fay sues` (`the day` 1 5 2026) EQUALS `not yet: I may apply once at least 120 days from the day the proceeding was commenced have passed (s 17K(1)(b))` (`the day` 2 5 2026)
#ASSERT `Can I apply to appoint an associated trust question` `the institution nominated one and the court has not yet decided` `Fay sues` (`the day` 2 5 2026) EQUALS `not yet: the court has not decided the institution's nomination (s 17K(1)(a)(ii))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to appoint an associated trust question` `the court appointed the proper respondent the institution nominated` `Fay sues` (`the day` 2 5 2026) EQUALS `no: the court has appointed the proper respondent the institution nominated, so section 17K(1)(a) is not met`

-- s 17K(3): Fay applies on 2 May 2026; the institution has until 30 May 2026 (2 May + 28).
#ASSERT `By when must the institution identify its trusts question` (`the day` 2 5 2026) EQUALS `the day` 30 5 2026
#ASSERT `days from` (`the day` 2 5 2026) `to` (`the day` 30 5 2026) EQUALS 28
`the institution answers on day 28` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 17K(3) -- the institution must identify its associated trusts within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the institution` `identify its associated trusts and give the court information on their financial capacity` 28))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `the institution answers on day 28` EQUALS TRUE
`the institution answers on day 29` MEANS
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `s 17K(3) -- the institution must identify its associated trusts within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the institution` `identify its associated trusts and give the court information on their financial capacity` 29))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
#ASSERT `the institution answers on day 29` EQUALS FALSE
#TRACE `s 17K(3) -- the institution must identify its associated trusts within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
