#ASSERT `Is it an associated trust question` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the trust is an associated trust of the institution (s 17K(4))`
#ASSERT `Is it an associated trust question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the trust is an associated trust of the institution (s 17K(4))`
#ASSERT `Is it an associated trust question` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: none of the circumstances in section 17K(4) applies, so the trust is not an associated trust of the institution`

#ASSERT `Must the court appoint the trust question` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court must appoint the associated trust as the proper respondent; it takes on the institution's liability to me (s 17L), but its liability is limited to the value of the trust property (s 17M(3))`
#ASSERT `Must the court appoint the trust question` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the court is not required to appoint the trust, because it is not satisfied of every matter in section 17K(2)`

-- Divisions 5, 6.
#ASSERT `Is the successor liable question` `it, or part of it, merged into another institution` EQUALS `yes: the successor institution is substantially the same as the former one and assumes its liability for my claim (s 17P(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Is the successor liable question` `a chain of such mergers and separations leads from it to the other institution` EQUALS `yes: the successor institution is substantially the same as the former one and assumes its liability for my claim (s 17P(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Is the successor liable question` `it only changed its name or structure, became incorporated, or changed the area where it works` EQUALS `yes: a change of name, structure or area, or becoming incorporated, does not matter; my claim is against the institution as it now is (s 17P(4))`
#ASSERT `Is the successor liable question` `something else` EQUALS `yes, if the court finds the other institution substantially the same as the former one (s 17P(2)); section 17P(3) does not list what happened`

#ASSERT `Whom can I sue question` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the institution itself: Division 6 of Part 3A is for unincorporated institutions, and this one is incorporated`
#ASSERT `Whom can I sue question` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `I may sue the institution in its own name (s 17Q(1)); and I may sue the current holder of the former office holder's office, in the name of that office, who takes on the former office holder's liability and defences (s 17R(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Whom can I sue question` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I may sue the institution in its own name (s 17Q(1)); and I may sue the head of the institution in the name of the former office holder's office, who takes on the former office holder's liability and defences (s 17R(2)-(4))`
-- The former office holder still holds office: s 17R(1)(e) fails; sue the institution (and that person directly).
#ASSERT `Whom can I sue question` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `I may sue the institution in its own name, as if it were a legal person (s 17Q(1))`
#ASSERT `Whom can I sue question` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `I may sue the institution in its own name, as if it were a legal person (s 17Q(1))`

