-- Part 4A. HYPOTHETICAL: Hal, a prisoner at Darwin Correctional Centre, is held in a cell beyond his release date.
`Part 4A applies` MEANS `yes: Part 4A applies: my damages are capped (s 32E), there are no aggravated or exemplary damages (s 32F), a public entity defendant may withhold what I owe for victims levies and fines (s 32G), and the rest is held on trust by the Public Trustee for victims' claims before it is released to me (ss 32H, 32M)`
#ASSERT `Does Part 4A apply to my claim question` `false imprisonment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`the day` 3 6 2022) EQUALS `Part 4A applies`
#ASSERT `Does Part 4A apply to my claim question` `false imprisonment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (`the day` 2 6 2022) EQUALS `no: Part 4A does not apply to a wrong from an incident before section 32B commenced (s 32B(5))`
#ASSERT `Does Part 4A apply to my claim question` `battery` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `no: Part 4A does not apply to a claim for damages for personal injury (s 32B(3)); the rest of the Act applies to that claim`
#ASSERT `Does Part 4A apply to my claim question` `battery` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `no: Part 4A does not apply to a workers compensation claim by an offender who was a worker (s 32B(2))`
#ASSERT `Does Part 4A apply to my claim question` `battery` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `any day` EQUALS `no: Part 4A does not affect a claim for a civil wrong arising from child abuse perpetrated against me (s 32D)`
#ASSERT `Does Part 4A apply to my claim question` `battery` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `no: Part 4A applies only to a wrong sustained while I was an offender under the Correctional Services Act 2014 or a detainee under the Youth Justice Act 2005 (s 32B(1), 32E(3))`
#ASSERT `Does Part 4A apply to my claim question` `another civil wrong (for example negligence)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `no: Part 4A applies only to assault, battery and false imprisonment (ss 32A, 32B(4))`

