-- ss 32G, 32H, 32M. Hal is awarded $10 000 on 31 March 2026; he owes $1 500 victims levy and $500 in fines.
`Hal's award` MEANS `the day` 31 3 2026
#ASSERT `What happens to my damages question` 10000 TRUE 1500 500 `Hal's award` FALSE EQUALS `What happens to my damages` WITH `the most the public entity may withhold for what I owe` IS 2000, `paid to the Public Trustee to hold on trust` IS 8000, `when the trust ends` IS `the trust period ends on the date given; what remains is then released to me (s 32M)` (`the day` 31 3 2027)
#ASSERT `What happens to my damages question` 10000 TRUE 1500 500 `Hal's award` TRUE EQUALS `What happens to my damages` WITH `the most the public entity may withhold for what I owe` IS 2000, `paid to the Public Trustee to hold on trust` IS 8000, `when the trust ends` IS `the trust period ends on the later of the date given and the day the victim claims are finally determined; what remains is then released to me (s 32M)` (`the day` 31 3 2027)
-- A private defendant cannot withhold (s 32G is for public entity defendants), but the damages still go to the Public Trustee (s 32H).
#ASSERT `What happens to my damages question` 10000 FALSE 1500 500 `Hal's award` FALSE EQUALS `What happens to my damages` WITH `the most the public entity may withhold for what I owe` IS 0, `paid to the Public Trustee to hold on trust` IS 10000, `when the trust ends` IS `the trust period ends on the date given; what remains is then released to me (s 32M)` (`the day` 31 3 2027)
-- Debts larger than the award.
#ASSERT `What happens to my damages question` 10000 TRUE 9000 3000 `Hal's award` FALSE EQUALS `What happens to my damages` WITH `the most the public entity may withhold for what I owe` IS 10000, `paid to the Public Trustee to hold on trust` IS 0, `when the trust ends` IS `the trust period ends on the date given; what remains is then released to me (s 32M)` (`the day` 31 3 2027)
-- 12 months after 29 February 2024 is 28 February 2025; after 31 May 2026, 31 May 2027.
#ASSERT `What happens to my damages question` 10000 TRUE 0 0 (`the day` 29 2 2024) FALSE EQUALS `What happens to my damages` WITH `the most the public entity may withhold for what I owe` IS 0, `paid to the Public Trustee to hold on trust` IS 10000, `when the trust ends` IS `the trust period ends on the date given; what remains is then released to me (s 32M)` (`the day` 28 2 2025)
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (`the day` 31 5 2026) EQUALS `the day` 31 5 2027

-- The victim: Iris, whom Hal assaulted in 2015 (out of time under the Limitation Act 1981 s 12(1)).
#ASSERT `Can I claim against the offender's damages question` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Limitation Act 1981 section 12(1) period does not bar my claim while money is held on trust for the offender (s 32P); if I succeed or settle, the court may order my damages paid from the trust, up to what is held, once all victims' claims are finally determined, in a fair and reasonable share (s 32K)`
#ASSERT `Can I claim against the offender's damages question` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `section 32P does not help: no money is held on trust for the offender under section 32H, so the ordinary limitation period applies`
#ASSERT `Can I claim against the offender's damages question` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `section 32P does not help: my claim is not a victim claim, because the conduct that injured me was not shown to be an offence (s 32A)`

-- s 32J(4), (5): Iris asks on 10 April 2026; the details are due by 8 May 2026 (10 April + 28).
#ASSERT `Must they give me the details question` TRUE TRUE (`the day` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `answered` (`yes: the public entity defendant must give me the amount held on trust, the offence, the number of other victims notified and any orders made, by the date given (s 32J(4), (5))` (`the day` 8 5 2026))
#ASSERT `Must they give me the details question` TRUE FALSE (`the day` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `answered` `no: a victim may ask only during the period the money is held on trust (s 32J(4))`
#ASSERT `Must they give me the details question` FALSE TRUE (`the day` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `not covered` `only a victim notified in writing under section 32J(1)(a) is given the right to ask for details (s 32J(4)); the Act does not speak to others`
